==> openstack.openhpc:    Cluster installation and protocol deployment
==> openstack.openhpc:       To install a cluster or deploy protocols with the IBM Storage Scale Installation Toolkit:
==> openstack.openhpc:       /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale -h
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:       To install a cluster manually:  Use the GPFS packages located within /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/gpfs_<rpms/debs>
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:       To upgrade an existing cluster using the IBM Storage Scale Installation Toolkit:
==> openstack.openhpc:       1) Review and update the config:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale config update
==> openstack.openhpc:       2) Update the cluster configuration to reflect the current cluster config:
==> openstack.openhpc:          /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale config populate -N <node>
==> openstack.openhpc:       3) Use online or offline upgrade depending on your requirements:
==> openstack.openhpc:          - Run the online rolling upgrade:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale upgrade -h
==> openstack.openhpc:          - Run the offline upgrade: /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale upgrade config offline -N;
==> openstack.openhpc:                /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale upgrade run
==> openstack.openhpc:       You can also run the parallel offline upgrade to upgrade all nodes parallely after shutting down GPFS
==> openstack.openhpc:       and stopping protocol services on all nodes.
==> openstack.openhpc:       You can run the parallel offline upgrade on all nodes in the cluster, not on a subset of nodes.
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:       To add nodes to an existing cluster using the IBM Storage Scale Installation Toolkit:
==> openstack.openhpc:       1) Add nodes to the cluster definition file:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale node add -h
==> openstack.openhpc:       2) Install IBM Storage Scale on the new nodes:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale install -h
==> openstack.openhpc:       3) Deploy protocols on the new nodes:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale deploy -h
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:       To add NSDs or file systems to an existing cluster using the IBM Storage Scale Installation Toolkit:
==> openstack.openhpc:       1) Add NSDs or file systems to the cluster definition:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale nsd add -h
==> openstack.openhpc:       2) Install the NSDs or file systems:  /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale install -h
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:
==> openstack.openhpc:       To update the cluster definition to reflect the current cluster config examples:
==> openstack.openhpc:          /usr/lpp/mmfs/5.1.8.2/ansible-toolkit/spectrumscale config populate -N <node>
==> openstack.openhpc:       1) Manual updates outside of the installation toolkit
==> openstack.openhpc:       2) Sync the current cluster state to the installation toolkit prior to upgrade
==> openstack.openhpc:       3) Switching from a manually managed cluster to the installation toolkit
==> openstack.openhpc:
